    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "Note",
      "title": "START HERE | Finished-image selective overlay, not AI editing",
      "pos": [
        0,
        1130
      ],
      "size": [
        1300,
        340
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 10,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "A = untouched original. B = the complete edited version containing changes you like.\nBoth must have IDENTICAL pixel dimensions and already share the same framing. This workflow will not silently crop, resize, shift or align either image.\n\nSAM: leave auto_mask ON and name the object in A whose area should reveal B. The retained default is watermark; change it to shirt, face, etc. instance_index -1 selects all matches. SAM does not generate new pixels.\nMANUAL: right-click ORIGINAL A, open MaskEditor, paint the parts that should reveal B, save the mask back to the node, then set auto_mask OFF. Do not paint on B. If SAM is unavailable, use this manual mode.\n\nNode 4: expand_pixels grows the selection; feather_pixels adds an OUTWARD fade. The fade is exactly zero beyond its finite edge. Invert selects the opposite area. For a hard exact mask use expansion=0 and feather=0.\nNode 5: an optional protect_mask input can hard-lock original pixels AFTER feathering. It is not a second required mask.\n\nQueue to save the full RGB photo in node 6. Other views are mask previews only. There is no Qwen sampler, VAE, edit prompt, crop/stitch path or transparent export. Changing the selection never regenerates B. This does not correct movement, color changes or lighting differences already present in B."
      ]
    }
